        "findings": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe membership-tier split (GOLD check first in `Owner.getMembershipTier()`, reading a transient `householdSize`) is well-placed: it keeps the tier derivation on the model alongside the existing `namesakeCount`-based logic, and the `applyHouseholdSize`/`countHouseholdMembers` scan helpers mirror the established `countNamesakes`/`countOwnersInCity`/`countOwnersRegisteredOn` pattern in the controller. No duplication there, and the controller is already the home of the household logic (`findHouseholdMembers`, `assignHousehold`), so counting by `householdId` there is natural.\n\nBut the insertion orphaned an existing Javadoc block:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:592-606`** \u2014 this Javadoc describes `assignHousehold` (`@param newOwner`, `@param lastName`, `@param address`, `@return the assigned householdId...`). The new `applyHouseholdSize` method (plus its own Javadoc at 607-614) and `countHouseholdMembers` (619-633) were inserted *between* that doc comment and the `assignHousehold` declaration, which now sits at line 635. The result is two stacked Javadoc blocks at 592-614, the first of which now visually documents `applyHouseholdSize` but actually describes `assignHousehold`, while `assignHousehold` itself (line 635) is left with no adjacent doc. A maintainer reading the file would find the doc/method association broken.\n\n  Fix: move the two new methods (and their Javadoc) so they do not split `assignHousehold` from its Javadoc \u2014 e.g. place `applyHouseholdSize`/`countHouseholdMembers` after the full `assignHousehold` method, or anywhere that keeps each method immediately under its own doc comment.\n\nEverything else about the structure is fine."
